
# Japanese KIND_PLUR (Phase 8) - limited coverage.
#
# Japanese doesn't mark plurality morphologically for most nouns - 母 means
# "mother" OR "mothers" depending on context. The singular-vs-plural surface
# differentiator the English KIND / KIND_PLUR split relies on isn't generally
# available. v1 covers the few cases where Japanese DOES mark plurality:
#   - explicit たち suffix on animate nouns
#   - inherently-plural collective compounds (兄弟 brothers / siblings)
# Singular kinship terms (母, 父, 兄) deliberately don't appear here, so they
# parse via the NP recall path (e.g. "私の母" -> the (o {?_I mother @o})
# recall -> tell_about, not tell_beliefs).
:KIND_PLUR

# Compound and たち-marked plurals. The たち forms are written with a space
# to match how the segmenter tokenizes them - 子供 and たち are separate
# dictionary entries, so "子供たち" input segments as ["子供", "たち"].
"兄弟"                  [k brother]             .
"姉妹"                  [k sister]              .
"兄弟姉妹"              [k sibling]             .
"子供 たち"             [k child]               .
"友達 たち"             [k friend]              .
"親 たち"               [k parent]              .

# Collective concepts - Japanese DOES mark these as plural-ish.
"興味"                  interest                .
"関係"                  [k relationship]        .
